{"id":"word:hebrew:H314","type":"word","title":"אַחֲרוֹן","subtitle":"H314 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"hinder ; generally, late or last ; specifically (as facing the east) western","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַחֲרוֹן (H314) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 51 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַחֲרוֹן (ʼachărôwn) means hinder ; generally, late or last ; specifically (as facing the east) western First listed occurrence: 1Chr 23 27."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַחֲרוֹן","transliteration":"ʼachărôwn","pronunciation":"akh-ar-one'","strong":"H314","lemmaId":"hebrew:H314","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["בָּ/אַחֲרֹנָֽה","וְ/הָ/אַחֲרוֹנִ֑ים","אַחֲרֽוֹן","וְ/הָ/אַחֲרֹנִ֑ים","אַחֲרֹנִ֖ים"],"morphs":[["HTd/Aamsa",12],["HC/Td/Aampa",9],["HRd/Aafsa",8],["HAamsa",8],["HAampa",7],["HTd/Aampa",3],["HC/Rd/Aafsa",1],["HRd/Aampa",1],["HC/Td/Aamsa",1],["HC/Aamsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"hinder ; generally, late or last ; specifically (as facing the east) western","usage":"after (-ward), to come, following, hind(-er, -ermost, -most), last, latter, rereward, ut(ter) most.","full":"H314. acharon אַחֲרוֺן 51 feminine אַחֲרוֺנָה plural אַחֲרֹנִים (also אַחֲרוֺנִים adjective from אַחַר , coming after or behind (as a comparative or superlative, according to the context); hence a. of place , behind, hindermost Gen 33:2 (twice in verse); הַיָּם הָאַחֲרוֺן the hinder (= the Western) sea (i.e. the Mediterranean: opposed to הַקַּדְמוֺנִי הַיָּם the front sea = the Dead Sea, the Semites, in defining the quarters of the heavens, turning naturally to the East, compare קֶדֶם of the East, תֵּימָן יָמִין, of the South, above under the word אָחוֺר d. and Assyrian mat a—arru 'the Western land,' of Phoenicia & Palestine) Deut 11:24 ; 34:2 ; Joel 2:20 ; Zech 14:8 ; Job 18:20 poetic אַחֲרֹנִים Ew Hi Di De the dwellers in the West (opposed to קַדְמוֺנִים ). More commonly b. of time , latter or last (according to context) Exod 4:8 ; Deut 24:3 ; 2Sam 19:12 ; Isaiah 8:23, of God Isa 44:6 (|| רִאשׁוֺן ) 48:12 (do.) compare 41:4 ; in Genl. subsequent (vaguely), א ׳יוֺם = time to come 30:8 ; Prov 31:25 (but Neh 8:18 ׳הָאַ הַיוֺם = the last day), (הַ)דּוֺר ׳(הָ)אַ the following Generation Deut 29:21 ; Psa 48:14 ; 78:4 ; 78:6 ; 102:19 , (הָ)אַחֲרֹנִים they that come after Job 18:20 (Ges Schl) Eccl 1:11 ; 4:16 , but Isa 41:4 the last , Job 19:25 יָקוּם עַלעָֿפָר וְאַחֲרוֺן and as one coming after (me) (and so able to establish my innocence when I am dead) will he ( גָֹּֽאֲלִי my Vindicator) arise upon the dust. — The feminine is used adverbially (compare רִאשֹׁנָה ) = afterwards or at the last (according to context): ( a ) absolute Dan 11:29 ; ( β ) בָּאַחֲרוֺנָה (opposed to בָּרִאשֹׁנָה ) Deut 13:10 ; 17:7 ; 1Sam 29:2 ; 2Sam 2:26 ; 1Kin 17:13 ; Dan 8:3 ; ( γ ) ׳לָאַ Num 2:31 (P) Eccl 1:11 .","rootNote":"or (shortened) אַחֲרֹן ; from 309 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 23 27","keyReferences":["1Chr 23 27","1Chr 29 29","1Kgs 17 13","1Sam 29 2","2Chr 9 29","2Chr 12 15","2Chr 16 11","2Chr 20 34"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":51,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 23 27","book":"1Chr","chapter":23,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אַ֣חֲרֹנִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Aampa"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 29","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הָ/אֲחרֹנִ֑ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Aampa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/אַחֲרֹנָֽה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Aafsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 29 2","book":"1Sam","chapter":29,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/אַחֲרֹנָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Aafsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 9 29","book":"2Chr","chapter